"""
The templates of tenants checked and rendered with Wolly.View at
run time, from the command line.

    view check DIRECTORY [DIRECTORY...]
    view render DATA LAYOUT PAGE DIRECTORY [DIRECTORY...]

check loads every file of the first directory whose name ends in .html or
.jinja, searching the directories in their order, as a tenant's engine
does, and prints ok or the error of each, then how many loaded; it exits 0
when all did.  render renders PAGE inside LAYOUT (an empty LAYOUT renders
PAGE alone) with the JSON in the file DATA, and prints what it wrote, or
the error and exits 1.  The engine of both has the functions of
Wolly.ViewFunctions, asset without a directory (the path as it is, as
a template engine without asset directories gives it) and t without a catalog (the key).
"""
module Wolly.Example.ViewTool is
    """
    The command of the arguments.
    No contract: the outcome is the result of I/O.
    """
    function main(root: RootCapability): ExitCode;
end module.
